IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.31 to 152.34: the other provisions of the Act that
-- apply to this Part, the delegation of the Minister of National Revenue, the offence, the regulation-making power and
-- the review of the Part.
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- Dates: the Act's text states no day on which Part VII.1 comes into force (s 190, piece ei6, does not name it), so the day on
-- which s 152.34's five years start is a plain input. No enactment or assent date appears in these sections.
-- This module imports no other ei5 module.

§ `152.31 Application of other provisions`

-- Subsection (1): all the provisions of the Act that are not inconsistent with this Part apply to it, with the modifications
-- the circumstances require, except sections 5 to 37, 48 and 56 to 65.2. The number of the section is read as a decimal
-- (7.1 comes between 7 and 8; 65.21 is after 65.2). Subject to subsections (2) and (3).
-- src:2652 | 152.31 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), all the provisions of this Act, except sections 5 to 37, 48 and 56 to 65.2, that are not inconsistent with the provisions of this Part apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.31(1) (src:2652)
GIVEN `the number of the section of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the section is inconsistent with the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.31(1) a provision of the Act applies to this Part` IF
        NOT (`the number of the section of the Act` AT LEAST 5 AND `the number of the section of the Act` AT MOST 37)
    AND NOT (`the number of the section of the Act` EQUALS 48)
    AND NOT (`the number of the section of the Act` AT LEAST 56 AND `the number of the section of the Act` AT MOST 65.2)
    AND NOT (`the section is inconsistent with the provisions of this Part`)

-- Subsection (2): subsection 86(1) (premiums and other amounts payable by an employer) applies as though "an employer" were
-- "a self-employed person"; subsection 88(5) applies as though "this Part" were "Part VII.1".
-- src:2654 | (2) For the purposes of this Part,
-- src:2655 | (a) subsection 86(1) applies as though the reference to “an employer” in that subsection were a reference to “a self-employed person”; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.31(2)(a) (src:2654-2655)
GIVEN `the person is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.31(2)(a) subsection 86(1) applies to the person as it applies to an employer` IF
    `the person is a self-employed person`

-- src:2654 | (2) For the purposes of this Part,
-- src:2656 | (b) subsection 88(5) applies as though the reference to “this Part” were a reference to “Part VII.1”.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.31(2)(b) (src:2654) (src:2656)
GIVEN `the matter is one to which subsection 88(5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 88(5) (piece ei3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.31(2)(b) subsection 88(5) applies to the matter as though its reference to this Part were a reference to Part VII.1` IF
    `the matter is one to which subsection 88(5) applies`

-- Subsection (3): section 102 (proceedings for offences) applies, with the necessary modifications, to (a) offences under
-- paragraphs 106(4)(a), (d) and (e) committed in relation to a provision of this Part or of regulations under s 152.26 or
-- 152.28, (b) offences under s 152.32, and (c) any matter referred to in ss 152.21 to 152.3 or relating to their application.
-- src:2657 | Application of section 102
-- src:2658 | (3) Section 102 applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in respect of
-- src:2659 | (a) offences under paragraphs 106(4)(a), (d) and (e) committed in relation to any provision of this Part or regulations made under sections 152.26 and 152.28;
-- src:2660 | (b) offences under section 152.32; and
-- src:2661 | (c) any matter referred to in any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or that relates to the application of any of those sections.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.31(3) (src:2657-2661)
GIVEN `the matter is an offence under paragraph 106(4)(a), (d) or (e) committed in relation to a provision of this Part or of regulations made under section 152.26 or 152.28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is an offence under section 152.32` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one referred to in any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or relates to the application of any of those sections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.31(3) section 102 applies to the matter` IF
       `the matter is an offence under paragraph 106(4)(a), (d) or (e) committed in relation to a provision of this Part or of regulations made under section 152.26 or 152.28`
    OR `the matter is an offence under section 152.32`
    OR `the matter is one referred to in any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or relates to the application of any of those sections`

-- Subsection (4): section 125 applies to (a) offences under subsections 135(1) and 136(2) committed by self-employed persons
-- and their offences in relation to contravening regulations under this Part (except those under s 152.26 and 152.28), and
-- (b) any other matter in this Part or relating to its application, other than a matter in ss 152.21 to 152.3 or in
-- regulations under s 152.26 and 152.28.
-- src:2662 | Application of section 125
-- src:2663 | (4) Section 125 applies in respect of
-- src:2664 | (a) offences under subsections 135(1) and 136(2) committed by self-employed persons and offences committed by them in relation to the contravention of any provision of regulations made under this Part, except regulations made under sections 152.26 and 152.28; and
-- src:2665 | (b) any matter referred to in this Part or that relates to the application of this Part, other than a matter referred to in any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or in regulations made under sections 152.26 and 152.28.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.31(4) (src:2662-2665)
GIVEN `the matter is an offence under subsection 135(1) or 136(2) committed by a self-employed person, or an offence committed by them in relation to the contravention of a provision of regulations made under this Part, except regulations made under section 152.26 or 152.28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is referred to in this Part or relates to the application of this Part, other than a matter referred to in any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or in regulations made under section 152.26 or 152.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.31(4) section 125 applies to the matter` IF
       `the matter is an offence under subsection 135(1) or 136(2) committed by a self-employed person, or an offence committed by them in relation to the contravention of a provision of regulations made under this Part, except regulations made under section 152.26 or 152.28`
    OR `the matter is referred to in this Part or relates to the application of this Part, other than a matter referred to in any of sections 152.21 to 152.3 or in regulations made under section 152.26 or 152.28`

-- Section 152.311 (delegation by the Minister of National Revenue to officers) is machinery: see NOTES.md, coverage table.

§ `152.32 Offence and punishment`

-- Every person who contravenes s 152.22 (the duty to file a return) is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any other
-- penalty, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 for each day the offence continues, to a maximum of
-- $1,000. Read: the fine is at least $25 a day but never more than $1,000 in all (fork F25).
-- src:2673 | 152.32 Every person who contravenes section 152.22 is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 a day for each day the offence continues, to a maximum of $1,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.32 (src:2673)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 152.22` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.32 the person is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine` IF
    `the person contravenes section 152.22`

-- src:2673 | 152.32 Every person who contravenes section 152.22 is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 a day for each day the offence continues, to a maximum of $1,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.32 (src:2673)
GIVEN `the number of days the offence continues` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.32 the least fine on summary conviction` IS
    min (25 TIMES `the number of days the offence continues`) 1000

-- src:2673 | 152.32 Every person who contravenes section 152.22 is guilty of an offence and, in addition to any penalty otherwise provided, is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $25 a day for each day the offence continues, to a maximum of $1,000.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.32 (src:2673)
`s 152.32 the greatest fine on summary conviction` MEANS 1000

§ `152.34 Review of this Part`

-- Five years after the day on which this Part comes into force, the Minister (of Employment and Social Development: the keel's
-- `Party` constructor `the Minister`) must cause a review of this Part and its administration and operation to be conducted. A
-- duty of the Minister to cause a review; it gives the person nothing to claim, and the day is the only fact.
-- src:2687 | 152.34 Five years after the day on which this Part comes into force, the Minister must cause a review of this Part and its administration and operation to be conducted.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.34 (src:2687)
GIVEN `the day on which this Part comes into force` IS A DATE   -- the Act's text states no such day; piece ei6, s 190, does not name Part VII.1
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.34 the day five years after the day on which this Part comes into force` IS
    `add years` `the day on which this Part comes into force` 5

-- src:2687 | 152.34 Five years after the day on which this Part comes into force, the Minister must cause a review of this Part and its administration and operation to be conducted.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.34 (src:2687)
`s 152.34 the party who must cause the review to be conducted` MEANS `the Minister`
